    <name>
      <text>4.3 Reverse and Compound Percentages</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><span lang="EN-GB">Tania buys a laptop.</span></p>

<p><span lang="EN-GB">She gets a discount of 5% off the normal price.</span></p>

<p><span lang="EN-GB">Tania pays £\({@dispdp(aa,0)@}\) for the laptop.</span></p><p></p><p></p><p><br></p><p>(a) Work out the normal price of the laptop.</p><p>£[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p align="right"><b>(1)</b></p><p></p><p><span lang="EN-GB">Joan invests £\({@bb@}\)&nbsp;in a savings account.</span></p>

<p><span lang="EN-GB">The savings account pays compound interest at a
rate of</span></p><p><span lang="EN-GB">\({@dispdp(cc,1)@}\)% in the first year<br></span></p><p><span lang="EN-GB">\({@dispdp(dd,1)@}\)% for each extra year.<br></span></p><p><span lang="EN-GB"><br></span></p><p><span lang="EN-GB"></span></p><p><span lang="EN-GB">(b) Work out the value of Joan’s investment at the end
of the first year.</span></p><p>£[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p align="right"><b>(1)</b></p><p>(c) Work out the value of Joan’s investment at the end of 3 years.<br></p><p>£[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p><p align="right"><b>(2)</b></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
